    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (73.39) and **Christian Yelich** (69.09) anchoring the lineup as the premier starts. **Yordan Alvarez** overcomes a negative platoon split against Robbie Ray due to his elite 0.473 xwOBA, while **Christian Yelich** capitalizes on a favorable matchup against Zebby Matthews; the +13% platoon edge and the presence of a slow-delivery pitcher\u2014which historically inflates stolen base efficiency\u2014make him a critical asset for our 5x5 objectives. We are also leaning heavily on **Kyle Schwarber** (65.24) and **Colt Keith** (64.13), both of whom benefit from prime spots in the batting order and exploitable matchups against Jos\u00e9 Soriano and JT Brubaker, respectively. Despite a 33% rain risk in the game involving **Kyle Schwarber**, the +10% order bonus makes him too valuable to pull from the primary slots.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (54.65), who finished within striking distance of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (55.02). While **Carson Benge** offers a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the leadoff spot for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to capitalize on potential volume, even with a difficult platoon disadvantage against Daniel Lynch IV. We are also monitoring the status of **Kazuma Okamoto** (45.39) and **Trea Turner** (63.21) closely due to the aforementioned rain risk. While **Trea Turner** remains a high-upside play given his speed profile, he faces a slight efficiency penalty due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s proficiency in controlling the running game. If the weather reports deteriorate, we have depth ready with **Josh Smith**, though he currently sits on the bench behind our primary starters due to the sheer dominance of the opposing arm, Zack Wheeler.",
